  "id": "COMPOUND:30800 - PROTEIN:1267",
  "verbalization": "Tubocapsenolide A is implicated in the activation of Mitogen-activated protein kinase 3 (MAPK3) through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Tubocapsenolide A directly targets the CD276 antigen, which in turn is a target of various compounds, including 12-Oxooctadecanoic acid and (+)-7,7-Bis[(5R,7R,9R,10S)-2-Oxocadinan-3,6(11)-Dien-12,7-Olide]. These compounds, in turn, have a shared target of MAPK3. The consistent presence of CD276 as a common intermediate across different pathways supports a mechanism where Tubocapsenolide A may act as a modulator of the MAPK3 signaling cascade. The evidence is robust, with multiple pathways converging on the same target, suggesting a potential role for Tubocapsenolide A in regulating MAPK3 activity through CD276. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on CD276 as a key mediator in the interaction between Tubocapsenolide A and MAPK3.",
